{"id": "EUVD-2026-97054", "enisaUuid": "e2311dc0-0e6b-31d0-b40b-13cb8152bf65", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the PUT /sys/dict/editDictByLowAppId endpoint that allows any authenticated user to modify low-code application dictionaries. Attackers can supply a dictionary's low_app_id, obtained from GET /sys/dict/list, via the lowAppId parameter or X-Low-App-ID header to rename dictionaries and replace their items.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T14:33:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T16:58:53", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_edit_dict_by_low_app_id.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/system/controller/SysDictController.java#L854-L860", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sys-dict-editdictbylowappid"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2274-mgcg-m5j6", "CVE-2026-108880"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e6404deb-e9a3-33ff-9aef-209dda1a98a6", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5eec4858-0c90-3911-8c69-3b0baea46219", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}